Step 4 – Run the relevant OEM pre-check job from console
Phase 1 – SSH Key setup
 
•	Runs script - 1_PSU_patch_OEM_shell.bash against the target host as per list of servers in OEM group
•	This script validates whether SSH key setup for scp_user in centralized server – xusvga92409d002 is already present on target server against grid/oracle user
•	If SSH key setup for scp_user is not present, this step will configure it.
•	This is required to transfer software/script from centralized server in Phase 3.
 



Phase 2 – GET_LANDING_PATH
 
•	Runs script - 2_PSU_patch_OEM_shell.bash on target server as per list of servers in OEM group.
•	This step determines which mountpoint or filesystem has more space (excluding root mount) to copy software and create a work directory (PSU_PATCH) there to take relevant backups.
•	This step also performs cleanup of work directory (PSU_PATCH) to ensure old files are not consuming space.
•	This step creates a flag file - /var/tmp/PSU_LANDING_PATH which has the information of where the working directory is created for next set of tasks to know where to look for PSU software and other file location.
 

Phase 3 – Transfer_script_software
 
•	This step runs on centralized server – xusvga92409d002 to transfer software and script files from central location - /backup/ORACLE/PATCH to target server working directory captured on previous step - /var/tmp/PSU_LANDING_PATH
 
 
Phase 4 – HOME_BACKUP_OPATCH_UPDATE
 
•	This script takes tar backup of Grid / RDBMS / Oracle inventory location which is necessary for rollback operations if any issue happens during patching.
•	If backup files are consuming more space, it will proceed to compress the file using gzip before proceeding to next step.
•	Once backup is completed, it will replace the OPatch folder which should be of recent version for patching operation to work.
•	It will also perform cleanup on Grid / Oracle home to clear patch version files older than 1 patch cycle to release some space on filesystem.
 
 
Phase 5 – PSU_PRE_CHECKS
    
•	This step runs on target server which runs opatchauto command by taking a snippet of services running on server.
•	This script will setup the staging script copied from centralized server – xusvga92409d002 under /home/grid and /home/oracle by extracting SCRIPT_FILE_GRID and SCRIPT_FILE_DB respectively.
•	The file - auto_apply_ru_html_separate.sh will be called by this step to have the workflow related to opatchauto analyze executed on both Grid/Database home.
o	This will also capture current patch version applied in Grid and database home.
o	This will capture status of cluster resources running on Oracle Grid HA
•	Based on the result of pre-check operation, it sends a mail to oracle team DL - dl.Takeda.Oracle.Dba@takeda.com 
•	It will also create and update a flag file under work directory with status of precheck operation.
 
 
 
 









