Phase 1 – Verify Precheck status
 
•	This step verifies the patch files are present in working directory and validates whether precheck operation performed is successful or not.
•	If files are missing or precheck operation is marked as failure, the job will fail.
 
Phase 2 – Schedule Blackout Target
 
•	This step places the OEM agent and its underlying monitoring targets in blackout to avoid incidents being created during patching operation.
•	It also places crontab under oracle user in disabled state to avoid mails.
 
Phase 3 – Apply Operation GI Home
 
•	This step takes care of applying PSU patch by running script - auto_apply_ru_html_separate.sh on Grid Infrastructure home by bringing down the services on its own.
•	It also takes a snapshot of all services running on server prior to applying patch.
•	Once patch is successful, it will validate whether services that are online is matching with prior status. If any mismatch observed, the script will mark the operation as failed and send mail for same.
 
 
 
Phase 4 – Apply Operation DB Home
 
•	This step runs script - auto_apply_ru_html_separate.sh on RDBMS home by bringing down the services on its own.
•	It takes a copy of services running and list of invalid database objects prior to starting patch operation.
•	Once patch operation is completed, it will verify whether patch is successful and send a mail of patch status.
•	It will also validate the status of services and invalid object list post patching and if any difference is found, it will mark status as failed.
 
 
 
Phase 5 – PSU Post Check
 
•	This step takes care of removing the database monitoring from blackout and ensures crontab is enabled on oracle user





